From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:25:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: mediatek: build the MT6797 variant without the DVFSP
 handoff

The MT6797 EEM calibration check validates the DVFSP PPM snapshot and
policy, which the DVFSP handoff provides. A kernel without the handoff
cannot link the driver as a module. Refuse that check when the handoff
is not built, so the temperature path builds on its own; the check is
only reached from the handoff side.
---
 drivers/thermal/mediatek/auxadc_thermal.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/thermal/mediatek/auxadc_thermal.c b/drivers/thermal/mediatek/auxadc_thermal.c
index 9e0904fca..67babb75b 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/mediatek/auxadc_thermal.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/mediatek/auxadc_thermal.c
@@ -1203,6 +1203,9 @@ static int mt6797_eem_calibration_ppm_check(
 
 	if (!input || !input->ppm_snapshot || !input->ppm_policy)
 		return -EINVAL;
+	/* The PPM tables come from the DVFSP handoff; without it, no check. */
+	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MTK_MT6797_DVFSP_HANDOFF))
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 	ret = mt6797_dvfsp_ppm_snapshot_validate(input->ppm_snapshot);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
-- 
